# 19. Comparison With Wildlife & Biodiversity

The two completed pillars now provide a useful cross-system comparison.

| Function                | Wildlife                               | Fisheries                                  |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Detection               | Five-year reviews, surveys, monitoring | Stock assessments, surveys                 |
| Early intervention      | State Wildlife Action Plans            | Harvest management before severe depletion |
| Legal protection        | ESA listing                            | Fishery management requirements            |
| Biological targets      | Recovery criteria                      | Reference points                           |
| Intervention            | Recovery actions                       | Catch/effort/habitat measures              |
| Assessment cycle        | Less standardized                      | Highly institutionalized                   |
| Performance indicator   | More fragmented                        | FSSI/status categories                     |
| Recovery                | Delisting/downlisting                  | Rebuilding                                 |
| Maintenance             | Post-delisting monitoring              | Continued management                       |
| Uncertainty             | Significant                            | Explicitly incorporated                    |
| Ecological scale        | Often multi-jurisdictional             | Often multi-jurisdictional                 |
| Major interface problem | Habitat/governance fragmentation       | Habitat/governance fragmentation           |

The comparison suggests that neither system contains a complete conservation model.

Instead, they contain complementary institutional strengths.

